      "body": "## Result\n\nThis source-bound contact moves the 902/1091 interaction from chart 618 to chart 373 and removes one paid MOVE on #7624. For the unchanged 17-call signed caller, the complete paid count falls from 110,060 to 110,043, with 22,461 targets and surplus 1,424 unchanged. The local directed application supports **κ ≥ 0.003665370499 under the explicit stronger common U**; the lower-minus-#7624-upper margin is `318696811/10^15`.\n\nThe scientific source is #7624 at `3f231831e0bff0cc5241ec89e122d99132bddf52`, with baseline main `e54523517d0f03e58352e647c403a5af3e525a57`. Candidate canonical SHA-256 is `df521d552dc35de6271e67655e4f9c466bc9247d37a5196b85613870209106a2`. The package preserves the exact five edits, complete source and candidate evidence, 502-path signed-completion closure, nested predecessor closures, and source notices. [PROOF.md](research/p104-contact902-1091-on7624/PROOF.md) states the zero-normalized-row argument and verification boundaries.\n\nTask `p104-side-correction`, scope **changed**: qualify the fixed published contact on the 204-lifetime #7624 source. The nearest overlap is #7625 on #7623 (180 lifetimes); its gain is not added to this result. #7624 already includes the 902-at-595 stay-drop. This package supplies its missing contact, zero-changed-CLEAR comparison and fresh complete validation.\n\n## Assumptions and scope\n\nBoth source and candidate require the five inherited framework assumptions and a **stronger unimplemented common U**. U covers the whole private extent and reachable numerical residuals, atomic return and nonaliasing; the already charged 4,000-unit lifetime item must cover all assigned work. The model retains 32 scalar services per INIT/CLEAR, a normalized coefficient `2^20` per service, all original width, size and precision factors, and precision context cap 4,096. No actual provider, implication from #7624's original erasure premise, same-original-premise dominance, unconditional multiplication theorem, or selected-frontier adoption is claimed. The six matched-base CLEAR changes already present in #7624 remain an inherited applicability question; the contact preserves its exact owned rows and CLEAR forms.\n\nThe retained first gate compares 204 CLEARs, 700 owned interfaces, 455 owned scalar-stream operations and one COPY. The corrected checker distinguishes all remaining live rows from nonzero-row metadata and checks both 204-certificate sets. Native coverage includes the fixed 1,075-pair source/complete union, 1,073 candidate pairs and 12 changed-route pairs, with 512 forward and 512 adjoint columns. The signed check covers 17 calls, 3,112 protected-generator catalogue cases, 104 boundaries and 58 outer predicates. Catalogue coverage is not a separate independent inventory oracle. The seven-check source resource branch is derived from paired fresh native calculations; the source catalogue was not rerun, and the captured intermediate files are author observations, not independent attestation.\n\n## Execution and validation\n\nThe initial guarded qualification was interrupted after prepare and certificate custody. A separately authorized continuation freshly replayed certificates and passed native in 1,406.98 seconds; its signed preflight then failed because the pinned source shim left an audit log in the source package. That failure and its 566-byte, two-row audit are retained. A second separately authorized service quarantined the predecessor audit, completed signed and resources, captured its 849-byte, three-row audit after group cleanup, and restored the 34-file source inventory. Its controller reported 651.53 seconds and a sampled peak of 650,571,776 bytes; the earlier continuation controller reported 1,444.50 seconds and a sampled peak of 1,267,863,552 bytes. Samples are lower observations, not complete cost accounting. These separate service attempts are not a cold six-stage replay.\n\nLocal artifact checks passed: normal and optimized read-only integrity,