      "body": "**Conditional κ = 0.0036614625547**, ×1.00009831 over #7620 (SYLforge, conditional κ 0.003661102618151). Official `evaluate_recursive_power` bracket (256 bits) [0.0036614625547, 0.0036614625548]; exact crossing 0.00366146255478988.\n\n**Premises: exactly #7620's** (its five inherited assumptions, its 167-CLEAR reading, its fixed 17*68 = 1,156 banks); no new premise. Rows, end charts, owned data (47 owned MOVEs, 167 lifetimes, peak 50, all 1,018 owned observations) and all 167 CLEAR contents are identical to #7620's.\n\n**Edits to #7620's word** (77,194 -> 77,196 events):\n1. Courier (funded-return) move on 1445/1461, shears -2 and 2/3 (5-smooth, passes main's #7000 alphabet check): transit 1445 drops chart 755, courier 1461 gains the stop 757. Non-dyadic literal events 5,901 -> 5,903.\n2. Helper 226 re-stop 3->6->9 to 3->7->9 (chart 719 -> 906), its encode `990 -= 226` slid earlier to chart 260, plus a swap of two independent MOVEs into chart 260.\n\n**Price:** paid delta per 17 calls {1:+17, 2:+17, 3:-51, 6:+17}; paid positions 110,145 and S 1,424 unchanged; ordinary bill 785,022,672; precision 303/299/299. `compare_recursive_invoices` against #7620: uniformly_better. `evaluate_recursive_power`: new_cost_lower at C = 0.0036614625547, new_cost_higher at 0.0036614625548.\n\n**Checks:** `scripts/research_package.py --package research/p104-courier-restop-on7620` PASS; `check.py` core + columns PASS (exact replay, 167 CLEARs identical, 846 affected chart pairs x 512 forward + 512 adjoint Gaussian columns with absolute-phase checks, 31 rejecting controls); `price.py` PASS. #7620's native runner pins 837 affected pairs; this word needs 846 (10 added, (719,127) dropped), tested by our own `check.py` written from the description in #7620's files (read as data; no code from other PRs was run). An independent read-only audit found the word sound relative to #7620.\n\n**Caveats:** conditional on #7620's premises, void with #7620 if they are refused; #7620's full native/signed 17-stage application is not rerun here. No maintainer review.\n\n**Credit:** base word SYLforge's #7616/#7620; the courier pattern is the crowd's (#7244/#7274/#7314/#7334/#7480/#7481 authors, credited in our #7615 and #7617); see NOTICE. DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
