      "number": 7619,
      "title": "P104 findings (Nov 15): caller dying-role proofs, native lock laws, spec ledger",
      "head": "b04b27d50f48a51b9ef8a7821b09b509429f97a9",
      "state": "open",
      "body": "This package collects the proofs and laws our lanes logged on Nov 15, after #7606, #7607 and #7609. It makes **no κ claim** and ships no word. Credit: DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code.\n\nIt builds on the Nov 15 frontier words (our #7615 and #7617, lineage through Clear1nsight's #7612 and SYLforge's #7616), on the funded-return/courier conventions of the crowd chain #7480/#7481, and on the retag/slide edit family that goes back to #7277.\n\n**Caller (rho = 2 two-arm):**\n- **DYINGPAIR [P].** No root has a dying role pair or single under the tight counts T1/T2. The Floor matrix is nonsingular without nesting, and the triangular recursion never meets eigenvalue 2.\n- **SLACK [P].** The interval-capped line price corrects the pricer (nested B unchanged; lone extra roles price at most 0 and are closed). Extended Crossing Lemma. A rank drop across a death forces b_K > 0 on both sides.\n- **GAPLEMMA [P].** The Δ-Floor lemma kills every pair layout and every k = 0 layout (102 of 117). The 15 single-role layouts left have a proved ceiling of +1.15%. One standalone open question (the HANDOFF) decides them.\n\n**Native side (words of #7615/#7617):**\n- Laws: RELAY-DIAMOND, lattice lock, the dim-8 non-nesting tails law, and the compiler laws JOINT-SUPPLY, FRAME-FANOUT and ROUTE-DEMAND-IS-UNIT-LEVEL.\n- Bounds: the exact single-main reroute bound (equal to actual on 400/400 mains; forced D 1,811 of 3,950 D0/call), the helper-layer floor 944 (1,366 with the endpoint census), the zero-need relay census, and the D ledger by bucket.\n\n**Spec ledger (rounds 1 to 3):** which clauses are SPEC and which are verifier-only; new public registers are legal and a one-hop helper costs 0 κ; the fresh-register meet-twice (Sandwich) rule; S = 2·(104·16 − 17·56); mains are S-neutral.\n\n**Checks.** The validator re-runs four checkers (`dfloor_count.py`, `icap_check.py`, `dyingpair/step1.py`, `spec/shuttle.py`) against the vendored #7546 word and #7113 caller, and passes. The native census scripts are lane code shipped so each number is traceable; CI does not re-run them (they read frontier words as data). No other author's code is run.\n\nCaveats: the slack/dying results are model prices [C-param] and proofs in the NESTPROOF root model; no root of any slack layout has been built. The native laws are scoped to the stated frontier words.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
