      "state": "open",
      "body": "## Result\n\nConditional κ = **0.00365760025222** (exact crossing 0.00365760025222326; official bracket [0.0036576002522, 0.0036576002523]), **×1.0002658 over #7616** (SYLforge's W2 stationary follow-up, conditional κ 0.003656628302607).\n\nTwo courier (funded-return) moves on the #7616 word: 532/1464 and 226/990 (226's MOVE 260→719 slid earlier so courier 990 is co-present at 719). Per native call ADD +2, MOVE −2 (76,896 events both); paid delta {1:−1, 2:−1, 3:−1, 6:+1}, 110,213 → 110,179 over 17 calls, rank surplus S = 1,424, ordinary bill 781.33M, precision 303/299/299. One new strictly nested chart pair (719,127); no non-dyadic event added. Rows, end charts, owned data (113 lifetimes, peak 50, 68 labels) and all 113 CLEARs are identical to #7616's.\n\n## Official tools\n\n- `scripts/research_package.py`: PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE.\n- `compare_recursive_invoices.py` vs #7616: uniformly_better, strictly negative.\n- `evaluate_recursive_power.py` (256 bits): new_cost_lower at C = 0.00365760025222, 0.0036566283026, 0.0036545537006; new_cost_higher at 0.0036576002523.\n- `check.py` (exact replay, shears, CLEAR equality, κ, 20+ rejecting controls) and an independent Gaussian column test of 448 affected chart pairs (#7616's pinned 442 + the 6 pairs on the changed routes, incl. (719,127)): 512 forward and 512 adjoint columns, absolute phase, rank, wrong-phase rejection each.\n\n## Premises\n\nConditional on exactly #7616's premises: its five framework assumptions (native_all_columns, owned_erasure, compiler, precision_tape, analytic_recovery), its reading of the 113 CLEARs, and its fixed 17·68 bank allocation. No new premise. #7616's full native/signed application is not rerun here; an independent read-only audit ran the official #7000 native engines on the word.\n\n## Credit\n\nBase: SYLforge's #7616. Courier pattern: the crowd's funded-return PRs (#7244/#7274/#7314/#7334/#7480/#7481, credited in #7615). The same moves were first applied in our #7615 (on #7613, #7612).\n\nDreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
