      "state": "open",
      "body": "**Conditional κ = 0.00365455370060, ×1.00040975 over #7613** (κ 0.00365305686569; exact crossing 0.00365455370060381; official `evaluate_recursive_power` bracket [0.0036545537006, 0.0036545537007]).\n\n**Premise (inherited, nothing new).** Conditional on the CLEAR #44 content interpretation of #7608/#7612/#7613 (owned 1557 erases `{451:-1, 1495:1}`, `owned_erasure`). All 74 CLEARs erase exactly #7613's content.\n\n**Moves.** Four courier (funded-return) moves on #7613's word: S/D = 532/1464, 1250/1464, 226/990, 7/779. Transit register S drops a mid-chart visit; courier D, co-present with S at chart a, carries S's content through an invertible shear re-basis to S's next chart b, where the inverse shear decodes. The 226/990 move needs 226's MOVE 260→719 slid earlier (to just after its last chart-260 op, event 33350). The move pattern is the crowd's: Clear1nsight (#7244/#7274/#7314/#7334/#7481, and #7612 beneath #7613), rohanarun (#7480, #7277), CubeJerry (#7577), petalas (#7326). #7613 builds on #7612 and is vendored as the base in `data/`.\n\n**Result.**\n- Paid 110,247 → 110,196, S = 1,424. Rows (1,569), end charts, owned MOVEs, lifetimes, peak and CLEARs equal #7613's.\n- Three new public chart pairs, all strictly nested: (3,746), (719,127), (743,245).\n- No non-dyadic event added (5,901 as in #7613); the word passes main's #7000 alphabet check (5-smooth denominators).\n- Ordinary bound (17 calls) 778,647,060 < 1e9; precision bit bounds 303/299/299.\n\n**Checks.** `scripts/research_package.py --package research/p104-four-couriers-on7613`: PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE. `check.py`: PASS_FOUR_COURIERS_EXACT (exact replay, shear inverses, 3 chart pairs, invoice, κ, rejecting controls). `price.py`: PASS_PRICE (`compare_recursive_invoices` uniformly_better against #7613; `evaluate_recursive_power` lower at 0.0036545537006, higher at 0.0036545537007). An independent read-only audit found the word sound relative to #7613. The signed caller and outer predicates are not rerun (header, rows, grid and owned data are unchanged). No upstream maintainer has reviewed this.\n\nDreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
