      "state": "open",
      "body": "The requested absolute +0.001 improvement was **not achieved**. This contribution retains two reproducible, source-bound obstructions so that the same unsuccessful routes need not be repeated. No selected result, supplier invoice or predecessor word is changed.\n\nFor exact #7613, an optimistic all-dimension contact relaxation still has a strictly negative full signed moment at C=.0046502223357 (#7604 +.001): upper bound about **−362.9625** with fixed endpoints and **−306.0163** even with jointly free helper input/output frames and their coupled new target credit. A second explicitly tested point, .0046530568657, also fails. This permits arbitrary F2^9 contact subspaces and extra moves inside old stays; scalar dependencies, owned trajectories and caller remain fixed. It is not a global ceiling or an impossibility claim for all larger κ.\n\nSeparately, promoting nine rank-seven owned BIT caches cannot recover any nonzero joint new-input combination using additional chart0-only linear repair under the fixed original chart trace. Nine explicit kernel witnesses, checked backwards and forwards, prove this including arbitrary interleaving. The hypothetical target credit is therefore not booked.\n\nValidation: four bounded Python 3.12 standard-library commands registered in VERIFY.json; authenticated self-contained sources; independently implemented contact DAG/reverse DP and rational interval engine; exhaustive coupled-credit controls; direct BIT dual-witness and joint-stock controls. This does not rerun or claim full physical/native/caller/precision/compiler/outer supplier admission. #7613's inherited CLEAR-content premise is preserved as a premise, not discharged.\n\nOverlap checked against #7574/#7582 (old stays/finite contact palette), #7577 (fixed helper histories), #7122/#7124 (endpoint recharts), #7304 (fixed-bank BIT splits), #6726 and #7162/#7163. The distinct enlarged scopes and open next questions are in the package README and proofs. Canonical base: e54523517d0f03e58352e647c403a5af3e525a57.\n\nCredit: DreamingOfClouds #7613, Clear1nsight #7612, FanPUYen #7604, SYLforge #7603, ToikY #7546, Rohan Arun #7113 and all retained native/arithmetic authors. Prepared by Hao Yan (@FanPUYen) with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance, including separately scoped checking agents. No independent human or formal-kernel verification is claimed.\n",
