      "number": 7609,
      "title": "P104 follow-up: κ(k) caller law, cut/pocket lemmas, radix-3 and spec-challenge results, CLEAR-content freedom (no κ)",
      "head": "04c0476cea2e647e46f03ba860aed3d0b4075f85",
      "state": "open",
      "body": "Follow-up to #7606, #7607 and #7608. It collects the P104 results our lanes logged after #7606 shipped. Package: `research/p104-follow-up-findings`. It makes **no κ claim** and ships no word.\n\nEvery claim is tagged. [P] means proved in PROOF.md. [C] means an exact computation that a checker in this package re-runs. [C-lane] and [C-param] mean lane computations or prices that CI does not re-run. [S] means judgement, which is never claimed as a result. Work in progress (the network-compiler route, R3TILE and the continuing dual scan) is excluded.\n\n**Highlights**\n- **CLEAR content.** Under `owned_erasure`, what a lossless owned CLEAR erases does not matter, and every CLEAR of an endpoint-exact word is lossless (Rank lemma). This discharges #7608's premise and answers Q1 of `research/p104-6372-clear-form-gap` with YES. Exact certificates are included: 21 terms for #7608's CLEAR #44, and 97 terms for each of the candidate's CLEARs 17755 and 17756. [P, C]\n- **Separation hypothesis.** r_max < k_min applies after strictification, so it is not a gap. The gate passes for #7546, #7605 and #7608, and the #7000 control is reproduced. [C]\n- **t = −1.** The F₂³ toy is decided by two independent proofs (Pin/DNL/Charge, and Forwarding/Union/Duality). The Pocket Lemma refutes every F₂⁴ survivor. On P104, 8 hubs realise the cut floor M = 72, so our earlier conjecture \"M ≥ n\" is false in the frame model. Hubs still do not pay: the V-funnel lemma forces a public layer of rank ≥ 96. [P, C, C-lane]\n- **Callers.** The Crossing and Floor Lemmas show #7113's B is optimal among nested two-arm layouts. A junk role is a disguised ρ = 3 root, ρ ≥ 3 gains nothing, and β = 4g + 2. Nesting is proved only at the outermost and innermost stages; interior stages are open. [P, C-param]\n- **Decoders.** The residual identity gives C ≥ n for odd-denominator networks and C ≥ 16 at half level. The h = 10 decoder costs 57. Neither 1/3, fooling sets nor lifted labels go below 56. [P, C, C-lane]\n- **Radix 3 and the spec challenge.** A12 is the only over-conservative clause found. Odd-radix endpoint wrappers exist, but Lemma Z keeps the per-port +1. The decoder target is H, so every 3-integral decoder costs ≥ v = 112 and there is no crossing. [P, C, C-param]\n- **Shape.** κ is bounded in k, h and v. Self-application gives Δκ = 0 exactly, and one outer level is optimal. [P, C-param]\n- **Negatives.** Scoped negatives cover resonance knobs, non-linear ops, single-step anchors, symmetry and Grassmann cuts. The dual scan rediscovers #7603–#7605.\n\nThe README has an explicit **Corrections** section for our own earlier statements:\n- LITSWEEP2's swapped graphs.\n- SPLITK/QUTRIT's grade assumption, corrected first by WRAPAUDIT and then by O1SPLIT.\n- R3BUILD: target N was a porting error.\n- HUBCLASS refutes the M ≥ n conjecture.\n- The B-optimality scope is nested layouts only.\n- PROFILECHK's flag, and other artefacts.\n\n**Verify** (stdlib; minutes in total):\n```\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/p104-follow-up-findings\n```\nThis runs `clearform.py`, `sepgate.py`, `toy4.py`, `labels.py` and `oddradix.py`. Each has positive and negative controls, and the validator passes locally (`PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE ... outcome=negative-result`).\n\n**Credits.** The TOY4 S2 proof, CALLEROPEN, JUNKROLE and DECLIFT9 are DreamingOfClouds lanes; so is WEBS, and its Cut Lemma shipped in #7606. Swarm work referenced:\n- ToikY (#7546)\n- Rohan Arun / rohanarun (#7113)\n- SYLforge (#7603)\n- FanPUYen (#7604)\n- aliromman (#7605, word vendored as data)\n- CubeJerry (#6805, #7000)\n- unpaidmoon (clear-form-gap package, read as data)\n- Clear1nsight and the P104 lineage\n- the PR968 authors\n\nNo other author's code is run.\n\n— DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
