      "number": 7607,
      "title": "P104 toolkit v3: token-settled drop engine, frame-perp duality, fast exact replay, κ(k) caller law (no κ)",
      "head": "25f59a4f0c912db09a159076a48932ca427cf5e2",
      "state": "open",
      "body": "A reusable P104 toolkit of our stable, verified tools for the hosted-word format of #7546 and later. Every tool has docs, a CLI example and tests with positive and negative controls on vendored data (ToikY's #7546 word, Rohan Arun's #7113 caller, our #7601 edit list). **No κ claim.**\n\n| tool | what it does |\n|---|---|\n| `pricekit.py` | exact caller + native invoice, certified κ enclosure (#7546: S 1424, κ 0.00364841129479084532481164) |\n| `dualword.py` | frame-perp transpose: an exact involution that preserves the price (dual(#7546) is priced bit-identically; dual(dual) = id up to the one COPY) |\n| `tokdrop.py` + `modp.py` | token-settled drop engine: clean-mode stay-drop repair, premix settlement rank, exact build. It rebuilds our #7601 word **byte-for-byte**. On the dual it finds the main-902 drop at chart 595 (K = 0), which the primal engine cannot repair |\n| `accx.py` + `fastreplay.py` | admissibility against a base. Replay mod 2^61−1 with exact Fraction re-checks: FAIL is exact-confirmed, PASS is randomised-exact (~1 s on #7546) |\n| `lossless.py` | law DUAL: every lossy owned CLEAR in one pass; agrees with exact ranks on 400/400 random programs |\n| `nativeplan.py` | helper-plan extractor; #7546 recost 9,975.447669, 70,714 helper events re-emitted identically |\n| `validate.py` | one command: accx + lossless + the repository's `compare_recursive_invoices.py` / `evaluate_recursive_power.py` |\n| `kformula.py` | closed-form caller C(k) (C(17) = the #7113 caller), S(k) = 96k − 208, κ(k) peaks at k = 17, κ* = 1/((2h−1)k*), κ(k) → 0 like 1/ln k |\n| `layout_price.py`, `cap_check.py` | parametric mask-layout pricer [C-param]; crossing caps and the Floor lemma on the built #7113 B (CALLEROPEN, a DreamingOfClouds lane) |\n\nCaveats:\n- The word #7601 + 902@595 prices to κ 0.00364932638757719639692487, below the frontier #7605. It removes one owned observation and has not had an independent audit, so it is reported as tool output, not as a κ claim.\n- The `layout_price` ratios price hypothetical callers with hypothetical natives, not words.\n- Excluded as work in progress: the NETC2–NETC6 compiler route, the REBUILDKIT netc planners and `floor_report.py`.\n- Excluded as not self-contained: the RES-LAYER sweep, and the TOY5 pocket checker (needs CP-SAT).\n- Not duplicated: the Cut Lemma checker and the Clone/Rank toy shipped in #7606. #6170 covers the older #6030 lineage.\n\nValidator: `python3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/p104-toolkit-v3` → `PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE` (5 commands, ~6.5 min locally; numpy==2.5.4).\n\n— DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
