      "number": 7606,
      "title": "P104: the odd unit, paid per grading — one cost behind the decoder wall and the t = −1 park (no κ)",
      "head": "032b0e8fa1c17f0f4728fe8a37ae3af7e6d7540d",
      "state": "open",
      "body": "## Summary\n\nThis package collects one day of P104 research on the two fixed costs every redesign has hit: the decoder's 56 owned units per plane and the t = −1 park. It is organised in three parts:\n\n- **Part I.** The lemmas and theorems, each with a proof and an exact standard-library check.\n- **Part II.** Every route closed that day, stated as a scoped negative result with its reason and numbers.\n- **Part III.** The words we built that did not pay, replayed exactly against #7546.\n\n**No κ claim.** No new frontier word. Package: `research/p104-odd-unit-per-grading/`.\n\n**One cost behind both walls.** Both costs are the same **odd unit**, paid separately in each port's own grading σ_p.\n\n- o(N) = rank of N's σ-odd part, for any block, ring or port coupling.\n- t = −1 holds exactly when the σ-even part is singular (the Cayley form of the park).\n- Two ports never share a grading inside a word (05-layers.tex l.4–7, 86–91).\n- The odd diagonal (q·q = 1) forces both an UP and a DOWN decoder in every plane.\n- Every construction that tries to move the park elsewhere needs a **moved owned row**, about 1 unit per port per call against a break-even of 0.214. This is enforced by the Rank, Lock and Clone lemmas, Theorem W, NT, AS/VA, the lift law, the Freeze Lemma, the web-general Cut Lemma and the Commutation Theorem.\n\n## Main results, with scope\n\n| result | scope | tag |\n|---|---|---|\n| o(N) = rank Odd(N) | any size, ring or coupling | P + C |\n| Cayley form: ker(R + I) ≅ ker E, so t = −1 ⇔ the σ-even part is singular | any contract | P + C |\n| t_eff = ab/(cd − ab) | per port | P + C |\n| M45 = HOST(−1, ½) up to one free SCALE, i.e. the t = −½ B-port contract | | P + C |\n| The ledger is per grading; the isotropic q_a + q_b kernel is even in both gradings | | P + C |\n| ρ = 1 forces the park | root callers | P |\n| Rank lemma: no event raises full-state rank; a dirty CLEAR is lossless iff its content is in span | premise-free | P + toy C |\n| Lock Lemma, Theorem W (separate twins need ≥ 96 moved owned rows/call), Lemma NT, Lemma AS/VA, lift law, Freeze Lemma | | P + toy C |\n| One lift serves ≤ 8 pairwise-orthogonal ports | | P + C |\n| Commutation Theorem: walls hold for any enlarged same-frame op set | | P + toy C |\n| XRECALL lemma, Zone lemma, owned additivity (c ≥ 0.92/port/call under any sharing), wiring lemma | | P |\n| Cut Lemma: rank(O mod Π) ≥ def(𝒢) for any up-set of frames and any helper web | validated on CubeJerry's W6805 (def 0, 104/104) and a t = −1 feeder word (def 1, 104/104) | P + C |\n| Cut Lemma corollaries: every t = −1 port needs an owned ascent leaving its Y-end hyperplane; descending decoders + line feeders ⇒ M ≥ 104; M ≥ \\|F\\| + α(R) with α(P104) = 8 | | P + C |\n| UP + DOWN decoders forced at t = −1, so every decoder saving also applies at t = 0 | | P |\n| G/2 = 13·proj(range G); the full UP∘DOWN composition leaves exactly −12·I on diagonal + odd cells | | C |\n| Joint multi-call decoder rank ≥ 8k | | P + C |\n| Lemma A(acyc): rank certificates are blind to acyclic junk | | P |\n| Lemma B (mod-4 certificates) | half-integer rows | P |\n| Early-set cap \\|E\\| ≤ 5,408 − 43,264/(d + 8) | d ≥ 2 closed; d = 1 open | P + C |\n| Theorem F, Lemmas LIN, TR, 2B, Descent, RT | local re-solve on a fixed schedule | P + C |\n\n## Corrections of our own earlier statements\n\n1. **The \"one-rank law\" is the Fredholm alternative (Theorem F).** Our drop-repair engines reported \"every drop misses by exactly one rank\". With one right-hand side that is only \"infeasible\". The contact-minimality conjecture we built on it carries no structure, and the rigidity it described is schedule-driven, with no lower bound (Descent Lemma).\n2. **HALF18 (already commented on #7583).** The full-flag certificate minimum is not ≈ 18 = 2h. Exact frame certificates of rank 15 (E8-120) and 13 (P104) exist, with lower bound 8. #7583's proved bounds are unaffected.\n3. **Internal notes only, never in a public PR.** Duality is type-preserving: U builds are not duals of L builds. EARLYCAP part B is refuted by T1CANCEL. BYPASS's relaxed screens were optimistic.\n\n## How to verify\n\n```\npython3 -I -B research/p104-odd-unit-per-grading/odd_unit.py   # PASS_ODD_UNIT_PER_GRADING (<1 s)\npython3 -I -B research/p104-odd-unit-per-grading/e8laws.py     # PASS_E8_LAWS (~3 s)\npython3 -I -B research/p104-odd-unit-per-grading/walls.py      # PASS_WALL_TOYS (~70 s)\npython3 -I -B research/p104-odd-unit-per-grading/onerank.py    # PASS_ONERANK (~3 s)\npython3 -I -B research/p104-odd-unit-per-grading/cuts.py       # PASS_CUT_LEMMA (~40 s)\npython3 -I -B research/p104-odd-unit-per-grading/words.py      # PASS_UNPAID_WORDS (~80 s)\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/p104-odd-unit-per-grading\n```\n\n- All checks use the standard library only and exact arithmetic.\n- Each has positive and negative controls.\n- Part III ships every word as an edit list against the vendored #7546 word (or against W6805 for the feeder), with a pinned SHA256.\n\n| word | result |\n|---|---|\n| SEEDBUILD S1 | +21.34 D0/call, κ ×0.999069 |\n| relocation control | +16.82 D0/call, ×0.999268 |\n| Lemma RT swaps (mains 6 and 886) | κ identical to #7546 in every digit |\n| WINDOW8 merged window | X = x − y, Y = x + y exact on 8 ports; 201.12 D0/call on the window route; no κ (merged plane) |\n\n## Caveats and open questions\n\n- **Lane-only numbers.** Numbers tagged [C-lane] are exact computations by our lane code and are not re-run in CI. [C-param] prices come from our invoice tool, whose control reproduces #7546's κ and S = 1424. Neither is a new claim against the frontier.\n- **Open.** Whether one owned ascent can be shared between t = −1 ports. Up-set cuts allow it, and no realisation is known; an exact F2³ decision is in progress and not claimed here.\n- **Open.** The d = 1 early-set window.\n- **Open.** ≥ 6 replacement rows and the h = 9 wall (C ≥ 52).\n- **Open.** A rank ≥ 9 free-lift decoder network below 56.\n- **Not included.** A network-compiler effort is ongoing; nothing from it is included.\n\n## Credits\n\n- **Authors.** DreamingOfClouds, including the outside-session lanes DECZERO, COURIER, YYMIX, XBIRTH and WEBS.\n- **Fable-assisted analysis.** The Clone lemma, the b-family and M45 as the B-port contract, each reproduced independently by our lanes.\n- **Words used.** ToikY's #7546 is the base word. CubeJerry's #6805 word is used as data only.\n- **Referenced work.** SYLforge (#7603), FanPUYen (#7604) and aliromman (#7605) are the current frontier. Rohan Arun wrote the #7113 caller. The PR968 decoder file comes from its authors.\n\n— DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
