      "body": "## Result\n\nConditional κ = **0.0036490213053944204892137903671** (×1.0001672, +0.0167% over ToikY's #7546, κ 0.003648411294790; #7546 builds on our #7542 and Clear1nsight's #7334).\n\nThe word is #7546's with two exact edits. Main 134 climbs 0→3 in one MOVE (was 0→1→3), and main 100 climbs 3→6 in one MOVE (was 3→5→6). Premix ADDs at the empty frame {0} settle the helper tokens, and four correction ADDs restore rows 134 and 166. All 1,569 rows, end charts, the 74 owned lifetimes and their erased contents, the header and the coefficient grid are #7546's. Paid positions go 110,468 → 110,434, and S stays 1,424.\n\n## Checks\n\n- `python3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/p104-token-settled-drops` passes (`PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE`).\n- `check.py` (stdlib only) does the following:\n  - rebuilds the word from #7546's vendored word and the edit list;\n  - replays both words exactly from arbitrary inputs;\n  - requires rows, end charts and owned data to be identical;\n  - recomputes the invoice and κ, and reproduces #7546's crossing;\n  - rejects 6 controls.\n- `chart.py` checks both new chart pairs ({0}→3 and 3→6) on all 512 columns.\n- `price.py` runs the repo tools. `compare_recursive_invoices` reports `uniformly_better` against #7546. `evaluate_recursive_power` brackets κ between 0.0036490213053 (`new_cost_lower`) and 0.0036490213054 (`new_cost_higher`).\n\n## Caveats\n\n- The gain is small (+0.0167%).\n- The claim is conditional, with the same premises as #7546.\n- The signed caller and outer predicates are not re-replayed. The header, rows, grid and owned data are identical to #7546's, and the content erased at each owned CLEAR is identical.\n- The phase-free chart control is informative only for the 3→6 pair.\n- No human has reviewed the package.\n\n— DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
